      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-212616",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A = {2, 3, 8, 9}$. Consider the relation $R$ that expresses \"is less than\" ($<$) on $A$, and the relation $S$ that expresses \"has the same parity\" on $A$.\n\nThe relation $R\u2229S$ contains the pairs $(x, y) \u2208 A^{2}$ such that $x < y$, {{field-1}} $x$ and $y$ have the same parity. Thus, we have\n$8$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}} {{field-4}}"
